Fast, local semantic code search powered by Rust

Usage: codesearch [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  search  Search the codebase using natural language
  index   Index the repository or manage global index registry
  serve   Run a background MCP server with live file watching and multi-repo support
  stats   Show statistics about the vector database
  clear   Clear the vector database
  doctor  Check installation health
  setup   Download embedding models
  mcp     Start MCP server for Claude Code integration
  groups  Manage repository groups
  remote  Manage remote federation peers (other `codesearch serve` instances)
  cache   Manage persistent embedding cache
  hooks   Manage codesearch integration hooks (git worktree auto-index, Claude Code guards)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -l, --loglevel <LOGLEVEL>  Set log level (error, warn, info, debug, trace) [default: info]
  -q, --quiet                Suppress informational output (only show results/errors)
      --store <STORE>        Override default store name
      --model <MODEL>        Embedding model to use (e.g., bge-small, minilm-l6-q, jina-code) Available: minilm-l6, minilm-l6-q, minilm-l12, minilm-l12-q, paraphrase-minilm, bge-small, bge-small-q, bge-base, nomic-v1, nomic-v1.5, nomic-v1.5-q, jina-code, e5-multilingual, mxbai-large, modernbert-large
  -h, --help                 Print help
  -V, --version              Print version
